{
  // The tests need `bun:test`, and Bun's types cannot share a program with
  // `lib.dom` -- both declare `DOMException`, `fetch` and a dozen other web
  // globals, and the duplicates are errors rather than a nuisance.
  //
  // That conflict is why this file exists, and it is doing a second job worth
  // more than the first. The session module is compiled here with no DOM lib at
  // all, so a module reaching for `document` -- or for `navigator.clipboard`,
  // which hangs off it -- fails to compile rather than failing review.
  //
  // **Timers are not covered, and nothing here can cover them.** #82 asks for
  // no DOM, no timers and no clipboard; this catches two of the three. Bun
  // declares `setTimeout` itself, as every runtime does, so there is no lib to
  // withhold that would make one an error. That third is held by review and by
  // the test asserting the session computes the same answer twice -- a module
  // that had scheduled something would still have to show it here to matter.
  //
  // `schema/tsconfig.test.json` is the same shape for the same reason: compile
  // the thing bare, because that is the only check that catches it reaching for
  // an ambient global.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "types": ["bun"],
    "lib": ["ES2022"]
  },
  // Both restated rather than inherited. `include` above is the whole app, and
  // `exclude` above names `test` precisely so the DOM config never compiles a
  // file importing `bun:test`; inheriting either here would leave this project
  // with nothing to compile.
  "include": ["test/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules"]
}
